{
  "sn22.55:0.1": "Linked Discourses 22.55 ",
  "sn22.55:0.2": "6. Involvement ",
  "sn22.55:0.3": "An Inspired Saying ",
  "sn22.55:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn22.55:1.2": "There the Buddha expressed this heartfelt sentiment: ",
  "sn22.55:1.3": "“‘It might not be, and it might not be mine. It will not be, and it will not be mine.’ ",
  "sn22.55:1.4": "A mendicant who makes such a resolution can cut off the lower fetters.” ",
  "sn22.55:1.5": "When he said this, one of the mendicants said to the Buddha, ",
  "sn22.55:1.6": "“But sir, how ",
  "sn22.55:1.7": "can a mendicant who makes such a resolution cut off the lower fetters?” ",
  "sn22.55:2.1": "“Mendicant, take an unlearned ordinary person who has not seen the noble ones, and is neither skilled nor trained in their teaching. They’ve not seen true persons, and are neither skilled nor trained in their teaching. ",
  "sn22.55:2.2": "They regard form as self, self as having form, form in self, or self in form. ",
  "sn22.55:2.3": "They regard feeling … ",
  "sn22.55:2.4": "perception … ",
  "sn22.55:2.5": "choices … ",
  "sn22.55:2.6": "consciousness as self, self as having consciousness, consciousness in self, or self in consciousness. ",
  "sn22.55:3.1": "They don’t truly understand form—which is impermanent—as impermanent. ",
  "sn22.55:3.2": "They don’t truly understand feeling … ",
  "sn22.55:3.3": "perception … ",
  "sn22.55:3.4": "choices … ",
  "sn22.55:3.5": "consciousness—which is impermanent—as impermanent